+// Chapter 34 checkpoint 3: fixed-step simulation and ping-pong slot ownership.
 //
-// After the reset pass, EmitCS allocates free slots from a group-scanned dead list, issues a monotone identity to
-// each spawned particle from a persistent counter, and seeds its position and velocity deterministically from
-// (seed, identity) so a spawn is reproducible on any adapter. Requested, spawned and dropped counters are the
-// honest capacity ledger: when more emission is requested than there are dead slots, the surplus is dropped rather
-// than silently overrunning. Simulation, compaction, indirect arguments and the checksum arrive in later
-// checkpoints, so emitted particles are not moved, retired, compacted or drawn yet.
+// SimulateCS reads a particle from the read slot, integrates it under the configured integrator and force field,
+// resolves the ground plane, ages it and retires it when it outlives its lifetime, then writes the result into the
+// write slot. Because a substep reads one slot and writes the other, the host ping-pongs ownership between the two
+// state buffers each substep, so a substep never reads a slot it is still writing. The died and contact counters
+// are the honest lifetime and collision ledger. Compaction, indirect arguments and the checksum arrive later, so
+// the advanced live set is still not compacted or drawn.
 
 #define LGP_PARTICLE_THREAD_GROUP_SIZE 256
 
